        <h2>Practical Information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Sigiriya:</strong> Opens 7am–5:30pm. USD 35 foreign adult entry. No entry fee for under-12s. Buy tickets at the booth before the water gardens. <a href="/places/sigiriya">Full Sigiriya guide →</a></li>
          <li><strong>Pidurangala:</strong> Opens 5am. LKR 1,000 (~USD 3) entry. No separate charge for the cave temple. Torch/headlamp essential for pre-dawn climbs. <a href="/places/pidurangala">Full Pidurangala guide →</a></li>
          <li><strong>Getting there:</strong> Both are a short tuk-tuk or walk from Sigiriya village. From Dambulla: 20km. From Polonnaruwa: 60km.</li>
          <li><strong>When to visit:</strong> December to April for dry conditions. Avoid midday regardless of season — heat is intense.</li>
        </ul>

